{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017kYyKn5P28WA914CjBN9U7","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer in the cluster mirroring design discussion.\\\\n\\\\nAccording to the file `/store/_intake/2026/04/30/mail-d143b0b41a8baaf69dfb3a1d-b13eb2ca.md` (lines 74-77), Federico Valeri, one of the KIP-1279 authors, states:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"AS27: Yes, add/remove along with pause/resume is confusing. We changed AddTopicsToMirror/RemoveTopicsFromMirror to **StartMirrorTopics/StopMirrorTopics**. We will still keep the same semantics though. Stop can be used for failover or migration use cases, and pause for 'pausing mirroring without making the topic writable' (maintenance).\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Final RPC Names:**\\\\n- **AddTopicsToMirror** → **StartMirrorTopics**\\\\n- **RemoveTopicsFromMirror** → **StopMirrorTopics**\\\\n\\\\nThis renaming was done to reduce confusion between the concepts of adding/removing topics versus the pause/resume and start/stop operations in the cluster mirroring design.\\\\n\\\\n**File cited:** `/store/_intake/2026/04/30/mail-d143b0b41a8baaf69dfb3a1d-b13eb2ca.md`\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/03/06/mail-3ff994af98687f284b08fecb-d28df905.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/03/10/mail-5d73dbf07c94c92bd8490ec2-9c9c06e7.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/30/mail-d143b0b41a8baaf69dfb3a1d-b13eb2ca.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":26.29,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":130146,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":44927,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1111976,\\\"input_tokens\\\":74,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1651}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20fa2da4-2da3-48ab-8026-c5cd8e059dda","uuid":"fa89eec6-6a20-4b8b-bd22-db779c7d8d04","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:12:41.198Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the a